6. IoT
Definition
Internet of Things (IoT) is a system in which physical devices are connected to the internet to collect, exchange and process data.

Examples:

Smart home

Smart watch

Smart agriculture

Smart healthcare

Smart parking

IoT Architecture
Usually explained using 4 layers:

1. Perception Layer
Sensors collect data.

2. Network Layer
Transfers data using Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, 4G/5G, etc.

3. Processing Layer
Cloud/servers process and store data.

4. Application Layer
Provides services to users.

Flow:
Sensors → Network → Processing/Cloud → Application/User

