19. LED Blinking Without delay()
Instead of stopping the Arduino using delay(), use millis().

C++

const int led = 13;
unsigned long previous = 0;
const long interval = 1000;
bool state = LOW;

void setup() {
  pinMode(led, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  unsigned long current = millis();

  if (current - previous >= interval) {
    previous = current;
    state = !state;
    digitalWrite(led, state);
  }
}
Why millis()?
delay() blocks the program.

millis() allows Arduino to perform other tasks while waiting.

