25. Ohm's Law
Formula:
V = IR

Where:

V = Voltage

I = Current

R = Resistance

Therefore:

I = V/R

R = V/I

26. Voltage Divider
For two resistors:

Vout = Vin × R₂/(R₁ + R₂)

Used to obtain a smaller voltage from a larger voltage.

27. Current Divider
For two parallel resistors:

I₁ = I × R₂/(R₁ + R₂)

Current divides between parallel branches.

